<title>USA: Ford names Lincoln-Mercury marketing head.</title>
<headline>Ford names Lincoln-Mercury marketing head.</headline>
<dateline>DETROIT 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ford Motor Co said Monday it named James Rogers as general marketing manager for the Lincoln-Mercury Division.</p>
<p>Rogers, who replaces Carl Bergman, will be responsible for developing and implementing the marketing strategies for Lincoln and Mercury products.  Bergman was named customer service operations manager for Ford Customer Service Division.</p>
<p>Before joining Lincoln-Mercury, Rogers was a vice president of A.T. Kearney Inc.</p>
<p>		((-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
